{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Nginx backends on node1, node2, and node3 serve their respective node identifiers from `/` on port 5660.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct post-restart checks show Nginx active and enabled, listening on port 5660, and returning the correct identifier on all three nodes.","evidence_ids":["cmd-945f4ed2a253463e","cmd-be766350a04c4491","cmd-5d30b122d4ce481d"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"HAProxy on node4 serves HTTP on port 80 and distributes requests across healthy backends.","status":"satisfied","summary":"HAProxy listened on port 80, returned all three backend identifiers in equal rotation, and reported every backend UP with successful HTTP health checks both before and after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9772e5572e6142db","cmd-ee17540ac965437c"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"The HTTP service remains available when one backend fails and returns to full health after restoration.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A complete transition was observed: healthy baseline, node2 stopped with its listener absent, 30/30 successful requests through node1 and node3 while node2 was DOWN, node2 restoration, and recovery of the full three-member pool.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9772e5572e6142db","cmd-27bc2da77a22428f","cmd-1f72152372f44b0f","cmd-2232ac66e8e141e4","cmd-1a8e3c6888d84780"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Package installation and configuration built the requested service; the node2 stop/start was the bounded failover test and restoration; temporary response files were trap-cleaned; and all four reboots served the mandatory restart protocol. The guarded HAProxy original-configuration copy was a bounded rollback safeguard rather than experimental residue. The lone nonzero command was a read-only status probe interrupted by node1 reboot. Final snapshots show only intended listeners, no failed services, healthy package state, and no custom temporary residue. Every node has coherent pre-health, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, recovered service/content and pool state; fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate all four transitions.","evidence_ids":["cmd-a48d35c33132438b","cmd-e2bb894297ef4b2c","cmd-2b91aa441c7c46f0","cmd-ae4be087c6b64b40","cmd-945f4ed2a253463e","cmd-383a8de607d246fe","cmd-7ad0a422fcde41a2","cmd-320f8f48e59f42c8","cmd-be766350a04c4491","cmd-28a638d338fb45ae","cmd-5d7f5ce800c244c4","cmd-313f1b42ec9f4acc","cmd-5d30b122d4ce481d","cmd-9032d0b105b44d72","cmd-b067f97c27774259","cmd-6bb992bdb0404ed1","cmd-ee17540ac965437c","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:before_prepare:node2:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node2:boot-identity","global:before_prepare:node3:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node3:boot-identity","global:before_prepare:node4:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node4:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node4:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health","global:after_executor:node4:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The separate provider-wide restart protocol is complete and internally consistent for all four managed nodes.","limitations":["The bounded backend-failure drill used node2 as the representative failed backend; node1 and node3 were configured symmetrically but were not individually subjected to the same stop/restore drill."]}
